IMPORT prelude

-- Intoxicating Substances Act 1987 (Singapore) -- what an intoxicating substance is (s 2 and the Schedule), the misuse and supply
-- offences (ss 3, 4), the blood test and the presumption it raises (ss 13, 14), supervision and detention in an approved centre
-- (ss 16, 17), consent to body samples (ss 26A, 26B), deemed forfeiture (s 10(4)), body corporate officers (s 42), protection of
-- persons acting under the Act (s 41), and the penalty for each offence encoded (ss 4, 13, 16, 26B, 30, 31, 32, 38, 39).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/ISA1987.txt, with amendments to
-- Act 5 of 2025 (in force 9 March 2025) shown. The arrangement of sections at the head of the deposit is out of step with the body
-- from s 16 on (it lists s 16 as "Treatment and rehabilitation"); the body's section numbers are followed here.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 11 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. SCOPED to the rules a member of the public, a
-- retailer or a practitioner meets. Not encoded: protection of informers (s 6), arrest, bail, search and investigation powers
-- (ss 7, 7A, 8, 12), the information requisition beyond its offence (s 5), administration of approved centres and Review Committees
-- (ss 18 to 20), discharge, transfer and magistrate's inquiries (ss 21, 22), legal custody and use of weapons (ss 23 to 25), the
-- register and DNA database (ss 26C, 26D), committees of inquiry beyond their offences (ss 27 to 37), indemnity (s 40) and
-- regulations (s 43).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Intoxicating Substances Act 1987 -- misuse`

§§ `2 and the Schedule -- intoxicating substance`

-- s 2: "intoxicating substance" means "any substance having the property of releasing toxic vapours or fumes which contain any chemical
-- compound specified in the Schedule and which when inhaled induces or causes a state of intoxication".
-- The Schedule (Sections 2, 14(1) and 15(1)), first column / second column: "Toluene" -- "1 microgramme per 1 millilitre of blood."
-- [Act 5 of 2025 wef 09/03/2025]. Toluene is the only compound listed.
DECLARE Compound IS ONE OF
    toluene
    `a compound not listed in the Schedule`

GIVEN `the compound` IS A Compound
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the compound is in the Schedule` IF
    CONSIDER `the compound`
    WHEN toluene THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `releases toxic vapours or fumes` IS A BOOLEAN, `the fumes contain` IS A Compound, `inhaling it induces intoxication` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the substance is an intoxicating substance` IF
        `releases toxic vapours or fumes`
    AND `the compound is in the Schedule` `the fumes contain`
    AND `inhaling it induces intoxication`

§§ `3 and 39 -- misuse`

-- s 3(1): "A person must not, for the purpose of inducing or causing in himself or herself a state of intoxication, use or inhale
-- any intoxicating substance." (2): contravention is an offence. No penalty is stated, so s 39 applies: a fine not exceeding $2,000
-- or imprisonment not exceeding 6 months or both.
GIVEN `used or inhaled an intoxicating substance` IS A BOOLEAN, `to intoxicate himself or herself` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the misuse offence is committed` IF
    `used or inhaled an intoxicating substance` AND `to intoxicate himself or herself`

§§ `4 -- supply`

-- s 4(1): a person must not "sell or supply or offer to sell or supply an intoxicating substance to any person if the person knows or
-- has reasonable cause to believe that the intoxicating substance is, or its fumes are, likely to be used or inhaled in
-- contravention of section 3(1) by the person to whom the substance is sold or supplied or by another person". (2): $5,000 or 2 years
-- or both. s 2: "supply" includes having possession for the purpose of supply.
GIVEN `sold, supplied or offered it` IS A BOOLEAN, `possessed it for supply` IS A BOOLEAN, `it is an intoxicating substance` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `knew or had reasonable cause to believe it would be misused` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the supply offence is committed` IF
        (`sold, supplied or offered it` OR `possessed it for supply`)
    AND `it is an intoxicating substance`
    AND `knew or had reasonable cause to believe it would be misused`

§§ `13 -- blood tests`

-- s 13(1): an officer of the Bureau, police officer, special police officer or officer-in-charge of an approved centre "may require any
-- person who has used or inhaled, or is reasonably suspected to have used or inhaled, any intoxicating substance for the purpose of
-- inducing or causing a state of intoxication" to provide a blood specimen. (2): not required if the registered medical practitioner
-- in immediate charge of the case objects that it "would be prejudicial to the proper care or treatment". (3): failing "without
-- reasonable excuse" -- $2,000 or 3 months (no "or to both"). (4): the officer must warn; if not, the court "may dismiss the charge".
GIVEN `was required to give blood` IS A BOOLEAN, `the treating doctor objected` IS A BOOLEAN, `failed to give blood` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `had a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `failing to give blood is an offence` IF
        `was required to give blood`
    AND (NOT `the treating doctor objected`)
    AND `failed to give blood`
    AND (NOT `had a reasonable excuse`)

GIVEN `failing to give blood was an offence` IS A BOOLEAN, `the officer warned of the penalty` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court may dismiss the charge for want of a warning` IF
    `failing to give blood was an offence` AND (NOT `the officer warned of the penalty`)

-- s 13(7): the consent of "a person who has attained 16 years of age" is "as effective as it would be if he or she were of full age";
-- (8) no parent's or guardian's consent is then needed. The section is silent on a person under 16.
GIVEN `age` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person's own consent to a s 13 blood test is enough` IF
    `age` AT LEAST 16

§§ `14 -- presumption of misuse`

-- s 14(1): a person "is presumed, until the contrary is proved" to have used or inhaled for intoxication if the s 13 specimen is
-- certified by (a) an analyst employed by the Health Sciences Authority or (b) a person the Minister appoints (Gazetted, (2)) "to
-- contain an amount of any chemical compound specified in the first column of the Schedule in excess of the amount specified in the
-- second column". "In excess of" is read as strictly greater than.
GIVEN `the compound` IS A Compound
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Schedule threshold in micrograms per millilitre` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the compound`
    WHEN toluene THEN 1
    OTHERWISE 0

GIVEN `the compound` IS A Compound, `micrograms per millilitre` IS A NUMBER, `certified by an HSA analyst or appointee` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `contrary proved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `misuse is presumed` IF
        `the compound is in the Schedule` `the compound`
    AND `certified by an HSA analyst or appointee`
    AND `micrograms per millilitre` GREATER THAN `the Schedule threshold in micrograms per millilitre` `the compound`
    AND (NOT `contrary proved`)

§§ `16 -- supervision`

-- s 16(1): if a s 13 blood test makes it appear to the Director that the person contravened s 3 "and that it is necessary", the
-- Director may make a supervision order "not exceeding 12 months". (2): also for (a) a person convicted under s 3(2), or (b) a person
-- discharged from an approved centre under s 21, again not exceeding 12 months. (3): where the (2)(a) person is imprisoned, the order
-- "commences upon the expiration of that sentence". (5): wilful failure to comply with a requirement -- fine not exceeding $1,000.
GIVEN `a blood test shows misuse and the Director thinks it necessary` IS A BOOLEAN, `convicted under s 3(2)` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `discharged from an approved centre` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a supervision order may be made` IF
    `a blood test shows misuse and the Director thinks it necessary` OR `convicted under s 3(2)` OR `discharged from an approved centre`

GIVEN `months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the supervision period is lawful` IF
    `months` GREATER THAN 0 AND `months` AT MOST 12

§§ `17 -- detention in an approved centre`

-- s 17(1): a person under or after supervision, arrested on suspicion of a s 3 offence, may be directed by the Director to be detained
-- in an approved centre "for a period not exceeding 6 months". (5): the Review Committee may extend "for a further period or periods
-- not exceeding 3 months at any one time". (6): no person under a (1) order "is to be detained ... for a period of more than 12 months
-- after his or her admission".
GIVEN `is or was under supervision` IS A BOOLEAN, `arrested on suspicion of misuse` IS A BOOLEAN, `the Director thinks treatment necessary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a detention order may be made` IF
    `is or was under supervision` AND `arrested on suspicion of misuse` AND `the Director thinks treatment necessary`

GIVEN `initial months` IS A NUMBER, `longest extension in months` IS A NUMBER, `total months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the detention under a s 17(1) order is within limits` IF
        `initial months` AT MOST 6
    AND `longest extension in months` AT MOST 3
    AND `total months` AT MOST 12

-- s 17(2): an approved centre may admit for voluntary treatment (a) any person who uses or inhales for intoxication; or (b) a person
-- "under 21 years of age" who does so "on the application made by either parent ... or by his or her guardian or by any person for
-- the time being having the custody or control". (3): not to be detained "for a period exceeding 6 months". (4): statements made are
-- not admissible in a later prosecution under the Act.
-- INFERENCE: (a) does not say who applies; it is read as the person's own admission, at any age. (b) is read as allowing admission
-- on a parent's application only for someone under 21.
GIVEN `uses for intoxication` IS A BOOLEAN, `age` IS A NUMBER, `applies personally` IS A BOOLEAN, `a parent or guardian applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `voluntary admission is possible` IF
        `uses for intoxication`
    AND (`applies personally` OR (`a parent or guardian applies` AND `age` LESS THAN 21))

GIVEN `months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `voluntary detention is within limits` IF
    `months` AT MOST 6

§§ `26A and 26B -- photographs, finger impressions and body samples`

-- s 26B(2): the powers apply to a person who, on or after 1 March 2006, (a) "is convicted of or is serving a sentence of imprisonment
-- for an offence under section 3(2), 4(2) or 13(3)"; (b) is under a supervision order under s 16(1) or (2); or (c) "is in an approved
-- centre pursuant to an order made ... under section 17(1)". A voluntary inmate under s 17(2) is not listed.
DECLARE Status IS ONE OF
    `convicted of misuse`
    `convicted of supply`
    `convicted of refusing a blood test`
    `convicted of obstructing an officer`
    `under a supervision order`
    `detained under a s 17(1) order`
    `a voluntary inmate`

GIVEN `the status` IS A Status
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `samples and prints may be taken` IF
    CONSIDER `the status`
    WHEN `convicted of misuse` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `convicted of supply` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `convicted of refusing a blood test` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `under a supervision order` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `detained under a s 17(1) order` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 26A(1) "appropriate consent": (a) 16 or older -- the written consent of that person; (b) 14 or older but below 16 -- the written
-- consent of "both that person and of his or her parent or guardian"; (c) below 14 -- the written consent of the parent or guardian.
GIVEN `age` IS A NUMBER, `the person consents in writing` IS A BOOLEAN, `a parent consents in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `appropriate consent is given` IF
        (`age` AT LEAST 16 AND `the person consents in writing`)
    OR  (`age` AT LEAST 14 AND `age` LESS THAN 16 AND `the person consents in writing` AND `a parent consents in writing`)
    OR  (`age` LESS THAN 14 AND `a parent consents in writing`)

-- s 26A(1) "body sample": (a) blood; (b) head hair with roots; (c) a mouth swab; (d) a prescribed sample. s 26B(5): no "sample of
-- blood" or "invasive sample prescribed under section 26A(2)" is to be taken without the appropriate consent. (4)(b): otherwise
-- reasonable force may be used on a person who fails to comply.
DECLARE Sample IS ONE OF
    blood
    `head hair`
    `mouth swab`
    `a prescribed invasive sample`

GIVEN `the sample` IS A Sample, `appropriate consent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the sample may be taken` IF
    CONSIDER `the sample`
    WHEN blood THEN `appropriate consent`
    WHEN `a prescribed invasive sample` THEN `appropriate consent`
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `10(4) -- deemed forfeiture`

-- s 10(4): "If there is no prosecution with regard to any article seized under this Act, that article is deemed to be forfeited on the
-- expiry of one month from the date of seizure thereof unless a claim thereto has been made before that date".
GIVEN `prosecuted` IS A BOOLEAN, `a claim was made in time` IS A BOOLEAN, `months since seizure` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the seized article is deemed forfeited` IF
    (NOT `prosecuted`) AND (NOT `a claim was made in time`) AND `months since seizure` AT LEAST 1

§§ `41 and 42 -- officers`

-- s 41: a person acting "in pursuance or intended pursuance" of the Act is not subject to civil or criminal liability "unless he or she
-- has acted in bad faith or without reasonable care".
GIVEN `acted under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN, `acted in bad faith` IS A BOOLEAN, `acted without reasonable care` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is protected from liability` IF
    `acted under the Act` AND (NOT `acted in bad faith`) AND (NOT `acted without reasonable care`)

-- s 42: where an offence by a body corporate is proved to have been committed "with the consent or connivance of, or to be attributable
-- to any neglect on the part of" a director, manager, secretary or similar officer, that officer is also guilty.
GIVEN `the company committed an offence` IS A BOOLEAN, `the officer consented or connived` IS A BOOLEAN, `attributable to the officer's neglect` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the officer is also guilty` IF
    `the company committed an offence` AND (`the officer consented or connived` OR `attributable to the officer's neglect`)

§§ `Penalties -- ss 4, 13, 16, 26B, 30, 31, 32, 38, 39`

-- s 39: any offence "for which no penalty is expressly provided" -- a fine not exceeding $2,000 or imprisonment not exceeding 6 months
-- or both. That catches ss 3, 5(4), 9 and 26. Express penalties: s 4(2) $5,000 / 2 years / both; s 13(3) $2,000 / 3 months, with no
-- "or to both"; s 16(5) a fine not exceeding $1,000 only; s 26B(4) $1,000 / one month / both; ss 30, 31 $2,000 / 6 months / both;
-- s 32 $10,000 / 7 years / both; s 38 $2,000 / 6 months / both.
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `misuse under s 3`
    `supply under s 4`
    `failing to answer a requisition under s 5`
    `obstruction under s 9`
    `refusing a blood test under s 13`
    `breaching a supervision order under s 16`
    `escape under s 26`
    `refusing prints or samples under s 26B`
    `disobeying a summons under s 30`
    `false evidence under s 32`
    `influencing a committee under s 38`

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `supply under s 4` THEN 5000
    WHEN `breaching a supervision order under s 16` THEN 1000
    WHEN `refusing prints or samples under s 26B` THEN 1000
    WHEN `false evidence under s 32` THEN 10000
    OTHERWISE 2000

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `supply under s 4` THEN 24
    WHEN `refusing a blood test under s 13` THEN 3
    WHEN `breaching a supervision order under s 16` THEN 0
    WHEN `refusing prints or samples under s 26B` THEN 1
    WHEN `false evidence under s 32` THEN 84
    OTHERWISE 6

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `fine and imprisonment may both be imposed` IF
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `refusing a blood test under s 13` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `breaching a supervision order under s 16` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE
